From: F93k draft audit
Subject: [control] omit only the UDP selector release wait

Counterfactual for F93jQuicSameLoopReleaseTest. Applied to b7b338a06a37ea204690adf816ff1ab7a3741b2b, this keeps child and parent physical close operations, parent close-future waiting, and the original close-failure aggregation. It removes only the selector-key deregistration wait in closeDialParent. The draft holds the event loop after physical closes, so dial completion should become observable before the loop removes the cancelled UDP keys; its pending-result assertion should fail.

---
diff --git a/libp2p/src/main/kotlin/io/libp2p/transport/quic/QuicTransport.kt b/libp2p/src/main/kotlin/io/libp2p/transport/quic/QuicTransport.kt
--- a/libp2p/src/main/kotlin/io/libp2p/transport/quic/QuicTransport.kt
+++ b/libp2p/src/main/kotlin/io/libp2p/transport/quic/QuicTransport.kt
@@ -636,6 +636,5 @@ private fun closeDialParent(owner: DialParent): CompletableFuture<Unit> {
                 CompletableFuture.completedFuture(Unit)
             } else {
                 owner.parent.closeFuture().toVoidCompletableFuture()
-                    .thenCompose { owner.portRelease.awaitRelease() }
             }
         }.thenCompose { it }
